 "notes": {
  "score": "Every metric is put on its declared [0,1] scale, never min-maxed over the models, so a column does not move when a model is added. A family score is the unweighted mean of its metrics; the summary score is the mean of the five reconstruction families, equal weight each.",
  "elo": "VLM Elo is Bradley-Terry over 2221 pairwise comparisons on the 200 tasks, 18 systems, displayed on the conventional 1000 anchor. Ratings normalise to the field's geometric mean, so a rating is a distance from the field's average and the whole scale moves when the field changes; only differences are comparable between two fits. Intervals are a 200-draw bootstrap over tasks.",
  "coverage": "A scene a model never rendered enters at the declared penalty rather than being dropped, so every column is over all 200 scenes.",
  "cost": "Mean US dollars and mean tokens per task over each model's 200 runs. Open-weight models are priced at OpenRouter rates.",
  "families": "VQA is reported and left out of the summary score: it is a semantic judgement rather than a reconstruction measurement."
 },
